<section class="section"><h2>Why test with this file</h2>
<p>A known duration for testing duration limits, progress bars, seeking and the minute-and-second formatting of a player.</p>
<div class="table-wrap"><table class="kv"><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Duration</th><td>1 min 0 s</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Bit rate</th><td>128 kbit/s constant</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Sample rate</th><td>44,100 Hz</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Channels</th><td>Stereo</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Format</th><td>MPEG-1 Audio Layer III</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Tags</th><td>ID3v2.3 (title, artist, album, genre)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
</section>

<section class="section"><h2>What to check</h2>
<p>After your application has processed sample-mp3-1-minute.mp3, confirm that:</p>
<ul><li>The duration is reported as 1:00, to within a tenth of a second.</li><li>Seeking to 0:30 lands half-way through, which holds for constant-bit-rate audio without a seek table.</li><li>The title from the ID3 tag is shown instead of the file name.</li></ul>
</section>

<section class="section"><h2>First bytes of the file</h2><p>The first 64 bytes of sample-mp3-1-minute.mp3 as a hex dump: offset, bytes, then the same bytes as text. The MP3 signature is 49 44 33.</p>
<div class="code excerpt"><pre tabindex="0"><code>00000000  49 44 33 03 00 00 00 00  00 77 54 49 54 32 00 00  |ID3......wTIT2..|
00000010  00 1b 00 00 00 53 61 6d  70 6c 65 20 4d 50 33 20  |.....Sample MP3 |
00000020  28 39 36 30 2c 31 37 37  20 62 79 74 65 73 29 54  |(960,177 bytes)T|
00000030  50 45 31 00 00 00 10 00  00 00 53 61 6d 70 6c 65  |PE1.......Sample|</code></pre></div></section>

