<section class="section"><h2>Verify your copy</h2><p>This file is created in your browser, so it has no direct URL for curl or wget. The bytes are the same every time and in every browser, so after saving it you can compare its checksum with the SHA-256 value above.</p>
<div class="code" data-lang="sh"><pre tabindex="0"><code>sha256sum sample-mp3-1-minute.mp3     # Linux
shasum -a 256 sample-mp3-1-minute.mp3 # macOS</code></pre></div>
<p>On Windows, run <code>Get-FileHash sample-mp3-1-minute.mp3 -Algorithm SHA256</code> in PowerShell. For scripts and pipelines, save the file once and keep your own copy.</p></section>

